// --- ArenaFrame usage ---
//
// VECSXP allocations (allocVector(VECSXP, n) and the child SEXPs stored in
// rlist) are heap-managed via std::malloc() and are NOT arena-backed.  The
// rlist VECSXP is the .Call return value from rpart() and must outlive the
// ArenaFrame that governs R_alloc/ALLOC scratch memory in the same function.
//
// However, rpart() — the function that calls allocVector(VECSXP, ...) —
// also uses R_alloc/ALLOC extensively for scratch arrays (rp.ydata, rp.xdata,
// savesort, rp.sorts, ddnode, ddsplit, etc.) during tree construction.
// Those scratch allocations ARE arena-backed.  Therefore, the .Call-entry
// wrapper for rpart() must declare ArenaFrame as its very first statement.
//
// Memory lifecycle for rlist (VECSXP):
//   1. allocVector(VECSXP, nout) — std::malloc for the SEXPREC node plus
//      std::malloc for the SEXP[nout] child-pointer slot array.  All slots
//      zero-initialized (nullptr).  Throws RError on allocation failure.
//   2. SET_VECTOR_ELT(rlist, i, child_sexp) — stores the pre-allocated child
//      SEXP pointer into rlist->data[i].  No allocation; pointer copy only.
//   3. Python receives rlist as the .Call return value.  Elements are accessed
//      by positional index:
//        VECTOR_ELT(rlist, 0) -> which3   (INTSXP; use INTEGER())
//        VECTOR_ELT(rlist, 1) -> cptable3 (REALSXP; use REAL())
//        VECTOR_ELT(rlist, 2) -> dsplit3  (REALSXP; use REAL())
//        VECTOR_ELT(rlist, 3) -> isplit3  (INTSXP;  use INTEGER())
//        VECTOR_ELT(rlist, 4) -> dnode3   (REALSXP; use REAL())
//        VECTOR_ELT(rlist, 5) -> inode3   (INTSXP;  use INTEGER())
//        VECTOR_ELT(rlist, 6) -> csplit3  (INTSXP, only if catcount > 0;
//                                          otherwise slot is nullptr because
//                                          SET_VECTOR_ELT was not called for
//                                          the catcount==0 path)
//   4. Python calls free_sexp_deep(rlist) to recursively free all child SEXPs
//      and then the rlist node itself.  free_sexp_deep in SEXP.h handles the
//      VECSXP case:
//        if (s->type == VECSXP || s->type == EXPRSXP || s->type == STRSXP)
//            for each non-null child: free_sexp_deep(child)
//   5. Python calls free_sexp_deep(rname) separately.  setAttrib is a no-op
//      in the fake runtime, so rname (STRSXP) is NOT owned by rlist.
//
// .Call-entry wrapper example (once fake_arena.h is available):
//
//   #include "VECSXP.h"
//   #include "fake_arena.h"
//   extern "C" SEXP rpart_entry(
//           SEXP ncat2, SEXP method2, SEXP opt2,
//           SEXP parms2, SEXP xvals2, SEXP xgrp2,
//           SEXP ymat2, SEXP xmat2, SEXP wt2, SEXP ny2, SEXP cost2) {
//       ArenaFrame _frame;   // frees R_alloc/ALLOC scratch at function exit
//       try {
